! ax4b_156_test2_lve.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 1256 ("----I256---
! LVE AND LVS CHECK.", banner PDF p.173), TEST 2, the LOAD VALUE
! EFFECTIVE test ("-TEST 2 CHECKS THAT LVE WILL LOAD CORRECTLY WITH 5
! LEVELS, AND UNDER ALL CONDITIONS."), and the routine's end:
!
!   PDF p.182  012532.00-012556.00  I563-I566: TEST 2A
!   PDF p.183  012556.40-012602.40  I567-I5610: TEST 2B
!   PDF p.184  012603.00-012623.40  I5611-I5613: TEST 2C
!   PDF p.185  012624.00-012651.00  I5614: TEST 2D
!   PDF p.186  012651.40-012676.00  I5615: TEST 2E
!   PDF p.187  012676.40-012731.40  I5616: TEST 2F
!   PDF p.188  012732.00-012767.40  TEST 2F (end), exit, the routine's
!                                   continuity check, end-of-program rows
!   PDF p.189  012770.00-012775.00  end-of-program rows, IC256, ICK256
!   PDF p.190  012776.00-013033.00  156K1-156K22, 100LC; 013035.00 1000
!   PDF p.191  013054.00-013063.00  BIT0-BIT7
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi; checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax4b_156_test2_lve_listing.py.  The prologue and TEST 1
! are decks/ax4b_156_test1_lvs.strap.
!
! WHY IT MATTERS.  LVE (Reference Manual printed pp.28-29, PDF 31-32) had
! only the manual and MCP's one-level bootstrap use behind it.  This is
! IBM's own test of it, and it checks rules the manual states but no
! deck had exercised from an IBM listing:
!   2A  LVE to an LV (156K3, "LV,$X0,156K2") found in external memory,
!       in index storage (LX,$X1,156K3 puts the instruction word in X1;
!       LVE,$X0,$X1 reads it there) and in the accumulator ($R, after
!       L(BU),156K3).  X0 must get 156K2's ADDRESS (KVI,$X0,156K2), not
!       156K2's contents (162543.34): the LV is not executed.
!   2B  as 2A, the first one through a second LVE (156K4 -> 156K3); the
!       IX-storage and $R cases load 156K3 itself, as printed (see
!       ODDITIES).
!   2C  LVE in $X1 (156K5 = LVE,$X0,$R) to an LV in $R, and LVE in $R
!       (156K6 = LVE,$X0,$X1) to an LV in X1.
!   2D  the width of the final address by the class of the instruction
!       found: VFL 24 bits (156K7, 013004.77); direct index, immediate
!       index, misc (EXIC), BRANCH ON INDICATOR and CB 19 bits; FP 18.
!   2E  the found instruction is not executed (L(BU),1000 must leave $R
!       zero); it IS index-modified (156K16 "L(BU),0($X1)" with X1 =
!       777777.77 gives 777777.77); a progressive VFL (156K18) is
!       index-modified but X1 is NOT stepped; the right half-word of a
!       word that is a VFL at the left (156K19+.32) gives 19 bits, and
!       the right half of 156K20 gives 18 ("RHW OF SWAP").
!   2F  LVE to LVI,$Xk (156K21+k half-words): only X0, the first LVE's
!       J, changes, never Xk ("ILLEGAL SELN OF IX k"); LVE,$X15,156K22
!       (LVI,$X0) must leave X0 zero.
!
! SIX SEGMENTS, each ending in its own "B,SSW" (TO SSIP): I563, I567,
! I5611, I5614, I5615, I5616.  With SSW a PASS halt the driver runs
! this deck six times: from END (I563) and with ENTRY= the other five.
! The continuity rows after each B,SSW, the routine's continuity check
! and the end-of-program rows (LX,$X1,(8)103.0 ... B,(8)45000.0, which
! leave the program) are transcribed and verified but never run.
!
! ODDITIES, transcribed as printed:
!   * TEST 2B's IX-storage and accumulator cases (I568, I569) load
!     156K3, the LV, exactly as 2A's do, though their comments say "LVE
!     TO AN LVE IN IX STG/RACC TO AN LV" ("13000.02 10", "13000.00
!     80 ..." -- 156K3 is 013000.00, 156K4 is 013001.00).
!   * I567's first failure exit is "SIC,SEN / BZXE,SERS" ("1304.32
!     C0"), where every other first exit is "B,SERS".
!   * TEST 2F checks X1 and X2 after the first LVE only, then does two
!     LVEs (156K21+.32 and +1.0) before checking X3.
!   * Comment punctuation is the page's ("IX9.", "IX 15" with no period,
!     "-TO SSIP" without one on p.184, "VALUE BITS" without one on
!     p.182).
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: all six segments PASS IBM's checks (PC 1410 =
! SSW, SEN 0).  Final index registers pinned (MODEL BEHAVIOUR, as is
! CYCLES):
!   I563  X0 0x57fc00000000000 (value 012777.00 = 156K2's address, not
!         its contents), X1 0x57fc03000001800 (156K3's word, by LX),
!         CYCLES 364
!   I567  the same X0 and X1, CYCLES 366
!   I5611 the same X0 and X1, CYCLES 311
!   I5614 X0 0xffffc00000000000 (156K13's last check), CYCLES 442
!   I5615 X0 0xffffc00000000000, X1 0x7fff0000000000 (156K17, not
!         stepped by 156K18's progressive mode), CYCLES 443
!   I5616 X0 0, X1 0, X15 0xffffe00000000000 (LVE,$X15,156K22 writes
!         J = 15 only), CYCLES 968
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (each in its own scratch copy of bsv/, all
! six runs, the two TEST 1 runs and the I48 run repeated; every failure
! below halts at SERS, PC 1416, with SEN naming the SIC,SEN taken):
!   C1 the 24-bit (Full) width gives 19 bits ({h[31:13],5'b0}) -> I5614
!      FAIL (SEN 0x565a00000000000, X0 0x581200000000000, CYCLES 98:
!      the VFL case, 156K7).  Nothing else moves.
!   C2 the found instruction is not index-modified (effAddrSigned(st,
!      a, 0)) -> I5615 FAIL (SEN 0x56c000000000000, X0 0, X1
!      0xffffff0000000000, CYCLES 183: the 156K16 case).  Nothing else.
!   C3 the result is written to X0 whatever J says -> I5616 FAIL (SEN
!      0x57c400000000000, X0 0xffffe00000000000, X15 0, CYCLES 936:
!      LVE,$X15,156K22).  Nothing else.
!   D1 the chain is not followed (lveChainTarget never Valid, so a found
!      LVE is refused) -> I567 FAIL (SEN 0x55c600000000000, X0 0) and
!      I5611 FAIL (SEN 0x561e00000000000, X0 0); I563 and the rest PASS,
!      as they reach no second LVE.
!   D2 the found half-word is taken from the wrong half (ea[0] == 1 for
!      ea[0] == 0) -> I563, I567, I5611, I5614, I5615 FAIL (first
!      SEN 0x557400000000000, 0x55c600000000000, 0x561e00000000000,
!      0x565a00000000000, 0x56c000000000000); I5616 PASSES: 156K21's
!      neighbouring half-words are LVIs of the same address too, so the
!      wrong half still gives 777777.40, and no register but X0 is
!      written by LVE,$X0 (C3 is what catches I5616).
!   The LVS injections (B1, B2; see ax4b_156_test1_lvs.strap) leave all
!   six passing.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model in the same scratch arrangement: all
!   nine runs PASS with the pins in run_tests.sh.
! Every run is failed by at least one injection: I563 (D2), I567 (D1,
! D2), I5611 (D1, D2), I5614 (C1, D2), I5615 (C2, D2), I5616 (C3).
! NOT discriminated by any injection here: TEST 2E's "not executed"
! check (156K14) and 2D's per-class 19-bit cases individually.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points SSW (PASS halt), SERS (FAIL halt), SEN/SENO
!     (data words SIC stores into), at the addresses PDF p.193's SYN
!     table prints.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41), so SEN
!     stays 0 on a pass and names the error entry on a failure.
!   * Notation only: "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")"; the label
!     glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I56.., I000, I00LC);
!     100LC's printed digit groups "0 000 011 770 025 700 000 000" are
!     written without the spaces.
!   * SENO SYN,SENO on p.190 (printed value "1311.00+") is not a
!     statement here: SENO is the substitute at 001311.00.
!   * 100Z (013034.00) and BIT8 up are not used and not transcribed.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.182, 012532.00-012556.00: TEST 2A (I563-I566)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)12532.0
I563    Z, $X0                        ! -TEST 2A, LVE SECOND LEVEL INST
        LVE, $X0, I56K3               ! -IS NOT LVE, LOCATED IN 3 MEMS.
        LX, $X0, $X0
        BZXVZ, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LVE TO A LV IN EXT MEM FAILS TO
        B, SERS                       ! -LOAD ANY VALUE BITS.
        B, I564
        KVI, $X0, I56K2
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LVE TO A LV IN EXT MEM FAILS TO
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -LOAD CORRECT VALUE BITS.
I564    Z, $X0
        LX, $X1, I56K3
        LVE, $X0, $X1
        LX, $X0, $X0
        BZXVZ, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LVE TO A LV IN IX STG FAILS TO
        B, SERS                       ! -LOAD ANY VALUE BITS.
        B, I565
        KVI, $X0, I56K2
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LVE TO A LV IN IX STG FAILS TO
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -LOAD CORRECT VALUE BITS.
I565    Z, $X0
        L(BU), I56K3
        LVE, $X0, $R
        LX, $X0, $X0
        BZXVZ, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LVE TO A LV IN RACC FAILS TO
        B, SERS                       ! -LOAD ANY VALUE BITS.
        B, I566
        KVI, $X0, I56K2
        SIC, SEN                      ! -LVE TO A LV IN RACC FAILS TO
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -LOAD CORRECT VALUE BITS
I566    B, $+1.0
        BD, I563
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B, SSW
        BD, $+.32
        LX, $X13, IC256               ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+, $X13, BIT2
        SX, $X13, IC256
!
